## Why This Question Is Asked

Tests the ability to design scalable, highly available job queues with tenant isolation and live rebalancing.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant sharding and hot-tenant handling
- Replica synchronization and consistency models (CP vs AP)
- Online shard rebalancing with lease-based ownership
- Delivery semantics (at-least-once vs exactly-once) and deduplication
- Failure modes, observability, and testing under churn

## Code Example

```javascript
// Acquire shard lease for a tenant
const shardHandle = await acquireShardLease(tenantId);

// Enqueue job to tenant's shard
async function enqueueJob(tenantId, job) {
  const shardId = computeShard(tenantId, job.id);
  const shard = await getShardOwner(shardId);
  return shard.enqueue({ tenantId, job, timestamp: Date.now() });
}

// Idempotent job processing
async function processJob(job, shard) {
  const acquired = await shard.acquireLock(job.id, leaseDuration);
  if (!acquired) return { status: 'skipped' };

  const processed = await checkProcessed(job.id);
  if (processed) return { status: 'duplicate', jobId: job.id };

  await executeJob(job);
  await markProcessed(job.id);
  await shard.releaseLock(job.id);

  return { status: 'completed', jobId: job.id };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes cross-protocol data governance: masking at the boundary across REST, GraphQL, and gRPC, driven by per-tenant OpenAPI contracts. It tests how to derive and enforce field visibility, roll out changes safely, and audit policy drift.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant field-level visibility across protocols
- Contract-driven masking rules derived from OpenAPI
- Central registry (Redis) for tenant/resource visibility
- Canary rollouts and rollout safety across services

## Code Example

```javascript
function maskVisible(obj, tenantId, contract) {
  if (Array.isArray(obj)) return obj.map(v => maskVisible(v, tenantId, contract));
  if (obj === null || typeof obj !== 'object') return obj;
  const out = {};
  const allowed = contract?.visibleFields || [];
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(obj)) {
    out[k] = allowed.includes(k) ? v : 'REDACTED';
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test contract drift and automated rollback when masking changes break clients?
- What metrics would you collect to detect masking-related regressions across REST, GraphQL, and gRPC?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical replay-protection patterns in multi-tenant SSO architectures, along with real-world token normalization from OIDC and SAML protocols, JWKS key rotation, and designing scalable validation endpoints.

## Key Concepts

- Token validation across OIDC and SAML standards
- Per-tenant JWKS rotation and SAML metadata caching
- Nonce-based replay protection with time-to-live (TTL) enforcement
- Internal JWT issuance including tenant_id, user_id, scopes, and nonce

## Code Example

```javascript
// Issue internal token with nonce (Node.js)
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

async function issueInternalToken({ tenant_id, user_id, scopes, nonce }) {
  const payload = {
    tenant_id,
    sub: user_id,
    scopes,
    nonce,
    iat: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000),
    exp: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 300 // 5-minute expiry
  };
  return jwt.sign(payload, getInternalSigningKey(tenant_id), { algorithm: 'RS256' });
}

// Validate nonce during token validation
async function validateAndConsumeNonce(tenant_id, nonce) {
  const key = `nonce:${tenant_id}:${nonce}`;
  const exists = await redis.setnx(key, '1');
  if (!exists) {
    throw new Error('Replay detected: nonce already used');
  }
  await redis.expire(key, 300); // Match token TTL
  return true;
}

// /validate endpoint - lightweight claim extraction
app.post('/validate', async (req, res) => {
  const { token } = req.body;
  const [header] = token.split('.');
  const decodedHeader = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(header, 'base64'));
  const tenant_id = decodedHeader.tenant_id;

  const claims = await extractClaimsWithoutFullDecode(token, tenant_id);
  return res.json({ valid: true, claims });
});
```

